{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes between the two lotteries. We compute the outcome differences between Lottery A and Lottery B. Lottery A offers 2000€ with 100% probability. Lottery B offers 3000€ with 50% probability and -3000€ with 50% probability. The pairwise differences in outcomes are: (3000 - 2000) = 1000 and (-3000 - 2000) = -5000. The sum of the pairwise differences is 1000 + (-5000) = -4000. For the other direction (A minus B), the differences are (2000 - 3000) = -1000 and (2000 - (-3000)) = 5000. Sum = -1000 + 5000 = 4000. The decision reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable (larger) sum of outcome differences. Thus, the sum of differences when comparing A to B is 4000, and when comparing B to A is -4000. The reason prefers A because 4000 > -4000. Therefore, the reason clearly applies and prefers Lottery A.",
