  "step_3": "The decision reason requires considering the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes. The individual does not mention or compute such a sum. Instead, the justification is based on a comparison of potential losses and gains in a qualitative, intuitive way — focusing on the 50% chance of losing 3000€ versus a 50% chance of gaining only 1000€ (which may be a misstatement; the gain in B is 3000€, not 1000€). The individual does not refer to any mathematical aggregation of outcome differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as defined. The reasoning is risk-averse and intuitive, not based on the sum of pairwise differences. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
